I want to conduct a multi-level multiple mediator analysis, but I don't know whether my code is right.

TITLE: 1-(1,1)-1 model with random slope (MSEM);

DATA: FILE IS data14.dat;

VARIABLE: NAMES ARE ID x y M1 M2;

USEVARIABLE=ID x y M1 M2;

MISSING=ALL(999);

cluster=ID;

 ANALYSIS: TYPE = TWOLEVEL RANDOM;

 MODEL:

%WITHIN%

  sa1 | M1 on x;

  sa2 | M2 on x;

  M2 WITH M1;

  sb1 | Y on M1;

  sb2 | Y on M2;

  sc | Y on x;

  %BETWEEN%

  sa1 sa2 sb1 sb2 sc M2 M1 x Y;

  sa1 with sc M1 x Y;

  sa2 with sc M2 x Y;  ( I don’t know whether here should be “sa1 sa2 with sc M1 M2 x Y”)

  sa1 with sb1 (cab1);

  sa2 with sb2(cab2);

  sb1 with sc M1 x Y;

  sb2 with sc M2 x Y; ( I don’t know whether here should be “sa1 sa2 with sc M1 M2 x Y”)

  sc with M1 M2 x Y;

M1 with M2;

  M1 on x(ab1);

  M2 on x(ab2);

  Y on M1(bb1);

  Y on M2(bb2);

  [sa1](aw1);

  [sa2](aw2);

  [sb1P](bw1);

  [sb2P](bw2);

 model constraint:

  new(a1 a2);

  a1=aw1+ab1;

  a2=aw2+ab2;

  new(b1 b2 indw1 indw2 indb1 indb2 conw conb);

  b1=bw1+bb1;

  b2=bw2+bb2;

  indw1=aw1*bw1+cab1;

  indw2=aw2*bw2+cab2;

  indb1=a1*b1;

  indb2=a2*b2;

  conw=indw1-indw2;

  conb=indb1-indb2;

  OUTPUT: CINTERVAL;

